#-------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EDI Stream layer mapping table for ics55
# Version: 0.1b
# Date: 19 Aug 2026
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------

#--------------------------!!!IMPORTANT NOTE!!!---------------------------
# This layermap was deduced from two places
# GDS data from the standard cells (Confirms MET1)
# GDS data from the IO (Confirms MET2~RDL)
# The code from ecc-tools, specially in
#  ecc-tools/src/database/data/design/db_layout/IdbLayer.cpp:131
#  src/database/manager/builder/gds_builder/gds_write.cpp:344
#  src/database/manager/builder/gds_builder/gds_write.cpp:365
# As you can see, the get_order() for gds_write is the GDS layer number.
# The GDS layer type is ALWAYS 0. This is a limitation of ECC and should't.
# How it works in other technologies that are not ics55? Well, lets say:
# "They just reworked the lefs" or "They are hardcoded"
# As for the actual layer number, is just an increment from _z_order
# Whatever it gets read from the tech lef file, that is what it goes.
# In any case, as for preview purposes, I think this is enough.
#-------------------------------------------------------------------------

#EDI Layer Name  EDI Layer Type               GDS Layer Number   GDS Layer Type
#==============  ==============               ================   ==============

